* @title Multi-line backtick literal feeds an inline JS LOAD
* @expect Hello|world|こんにちは|世界|สวัสดี|ชาว|โลก|A|café|in|Zürich|Naïve|isn't|it
* @nonstandard backtick raw strings and inline JS LOAD are snoflake extensions
* Exercises two snoflake extensions together: a multi-line backtick literal
* carrying JavaScript source, fed to LOAD as an inline helper. WORDS splits a
* string by Unicode word boundaries via Intl.Segmenter, keeps the word-like
* segments, and joins them with '|'. The input mixes spaced English with
* unspaced Japanese and Thai, plus diacritics and contractions, to exercise
* the segmenter rather than a naive split-on-blanks.
        LOAD('WORDS(STRING)STRING',`
            function (s) {
                var out = [];
                for (var p of new Intl.Segmenter("en", { granularity: "word" }).segment(s))
                    if (p.isWordLike) out.push(p.segment);
                return out.join("|");
            }`)

        OUTPUT = WORDS("Hello world! こんにちは世界。 สวัสดีชาวโลก! A café in Zürich? Naïve—isn't it?")
END
